     "Researchers in Abu Dhabi tested 60 students aged 16 to 18. Each student first read 60 trivia questions (for example, 'Which planet has the shortest day?') and rated how curious they were to know each answer. For each student, the 30 highest-rated questions were classed as high curiosity and the 30 lowest-rated as low curiosity.",
